Alessio Franconi, Ph.D., is a designer and researcher focused on the intersection between design and circular economy.

He is currently a research fellow at the Brunel Design for Sustainability research group of Brunel University, London. As a Fulbright scholar (2018/19), Alessio was a visiting researcher at the Rochester Institute of Technology, NY. He has experience in industrial design consultancy at Indesit Company, JP Industries, and various Startups; and international academic experience at Brunel University London, UK, University Iuav of Venice, IT, Delft Technical University, NL, Mimar Sinan Fine Arts University, TR, and California Polytechnic State University CA. In 2016, Alessio was recognized as one of the first Blue Economy experts in the world by Professor Gunter Pauli at the University of Pécs, H.
